  "description": "Minutes: how an action lives across meetings. A scenario in plain steps, with what must be true after each meeting is published. An assignment recorded in minutes becomes a numbered action that is carried onto every later agenda until it is completed or canceled; moving its due date needs a note and keeps the original date and a history; completed and canceled actions are never carried again; each action keeps its number for ever. People are named, not given ids. Dates are YYYY-MM-DD.",
